Sarah noticed water pooling under the water heater this morning. It is a 12-year-old 50 gallon gas tank. She turned off the cold-water supply but the floor is still wet and she is worried about the drywall.

Key facts
Address: 2140 SE Division St, Portland
Water heater: 50 gal gas, about 12 years old

Next steps
- Confirm the technician can bring a replacement tank
- Text Sarah the arrival window

Booked
What: Emergency repair
When: Tuesday, November 10 at 1:00 PM PST

Open the call:
https://desk.example.com/#call/call_demo_01?ws=ws_demo

Call back: +15035550142

Transcript
Maya: Thanks for calling Brightwater Plumbing & Heating, this is Maya. How can I help?
Sarah Chen: Hi, my water heater is leaking. There is water all over the basement floor.
Maya: I am sorry to hear that. Did you turn off the water supply to the tank?
Sarah Chen: Yes, the cold-water valve is off, but the floor is still wet.
Maya: Good. I can book an emergency repair today at 1 PM. Does that work?
Sarah Chen: Yes, please. This is Sarah Chen.

The recording is in Linedesk.

--

You get one email per call to Brightwater Plumbing & Heating. Change in Account settings › Notifications: https://desk.example.com/#account/notifications?ws=ws_demo

